1
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:03,419
Komori-chan, at this rate, we won't finish
preparing for the cultural festival in time.

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,720
Even so, we can't just sneak into
the school in the middle of the night.

3
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:08,540
Should we go to someone's
house to work on it?

4
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:09,640
In that case...

5
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:13,080
Oh, it's pretty spacious.

6
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:15,210
We have to get this done by morning.

7
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:17,770
We're probably bothering you, huh?

8
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:20,550
Three guys suddenly showing
up at your place like this.

9
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:22,020
It's fine.

10
00:00:22,150 --> 00:00:26,720
Besides, I want the cultural
festival to be a success, too.

11
00:00:26,790 --> 00:00:31,030
In middle school, my
friends used to tease me a lot.

12
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:33,320
Of course it's just a joke.

13
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:35,599
Like anyone would actually
have a crush on Mayama.

14
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:36,470
Yeah.

15
00:00:36,471 --> 00:00:39,770
To everyone else, it was
probably just a prank.

16
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,910
So, I'm really happy about
your feelings, Asamiya-kun.

17
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:46,240
Even though I want to believe it...

18
00:00:47,710 --> 00:00:49,710
I'm still scared.

19
00:00:54,350 --> 00:00:58,020
So, I'm hoping you can give
me a little more time to answer.

20
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:02,260
I don't mind waiting, no matter how long.

21
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:06,930
You don't have to force
yourself to give an answer.

22
00:01:10,270 --> 00:01:11,270
Okay.

23
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:14,050
On the day of the cultural festival...

24
00:01:16,270 --> 00:01:19,230
If it's alright with you, let's look
around together during our free time.

25
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:20,340
Yeah.

26
00:01:22,410 --> 00:01:23,850
I want to get some crepes.

27
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:27,220
Sounds good.

28
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:30,000
Mayama?

29
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,500
(Incoming Call: Mayama Ten (Big Brother))

30
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:59,480
- Hello?
- Ah, Asamiya-kun.

31
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:01,079
Good morning.

32
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:04,950
I'm sorry, but Hare probably won't be able
to make it to the cultural festival today.

33
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:06,350
Huh?

34
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:22,499
- Over here.
- Okay.

35
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:23,400
(Haunted House)

36
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:24,730
We still don't have enough stuff.

37
00:02:25,610 --> 00:02:26,880
What else are we missing?

38
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:30,620
Here, here, here.

39
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:33,120
- Oh crap, oh crap.
- I'll call you back later.

40
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,639
- Make sure you come!
- Thanks.

41
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:36,190
Why isn't Mayama here yet?

42
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:37,990
Did anyone hear from him?

43
00:02:39,390 --> 00:02:40,390
Nope.

44
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:41,990
Maybe he's still sleeping?

45
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,139
No way, he's not Sakaki.

46
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:45,140
Hey.

47
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:49,600
Please tell Hare to get
some good rest at home.

48
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,760
We've got everything under control here.

49
00:02:52,530 --> 00:02:53,540
I'm sorry about this.

50
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:56,540
Talk to you later.

51
00:02:56,910 --> 00:02:57,910
Wait.

52
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:00,280
Asamiya...

53
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:06,220
Don't tell anyone about my fever.

54
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:07,420
Huh?

55
00:03:08,620 --> 00:03:10,120
I'll figure something out.

56
00:03:10,550 --> 00:03:11,750
Figure something out? How...

57
00:03:40,850 --> 00:03:41,850
Oh no.

58
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:43,620
There's a huge crowd gathering outside.

59
00:03:44,250 --> 00:03:46,490
Do we just have to wing it without Mayama?

60
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:52,760
Are we still using this vampire costume?

61
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:56,279
Ah, that's the rejected costume.
Just leave it in the break room for now.

62
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:57,530
- Got it.
- Wait.

63
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:00,900
If...

64
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:07,740
If Mayama doesn't show up, I'll...

65
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:13,940
Sorry to keep you waiting.

66
00:04:57,100 --> 00:05:03,500
"After Moving Seats, The Boy Behind Me Has A Crush On Me"
(Episode 5)

67
00:05:04,430 --> 00:05:05,970
We're counting on you, Asamiya.

68
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:07,800
Yeah.

69
00:05:11,645 --> 00:05:13,460
By the way, who is that?

70
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:14,740
I don't know.

71
00:05:14,860 --> 00:05:15,860
No clue.

72
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:17,380
It's Sakaki in there, right?

73
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:20,080
What about the hospital? Did you go?

74
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:22,140
Yeah.

75
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:25,220
I took some medicine, so I'm fine now.

76
00:05:30,930 --> 00:05:31,930
Huh?

77
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:39,470
You're still a bit warm.

78
00:05:40,570 --> 00:05:41,970
You really shouldn't push yourself.

79
00:05:42,170 --> 00:05:43,210
But...

80
00:05:43,810 --> 00:05:45,370
It's not your fault.

81
00:05:46,310 --> 00:05:48,010
I'll explain it to everyone for you.

82
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:56,050
I want to give it my best shot.

83
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:04,530
After all, we all worked so
hard to prepare this together.

84
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:07,460
Try putting this on.

85
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,670
Did I scare you?

86
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:18,350
If I can stick it out to
the end and finish this...

87
00:06:18,470 --> 00:06:24,580
I think I might be able
to like myself a little more.

88
00:06:28,550 --> 00:06:29,580
Please.

89
00:06:36,730 --> 00:06:38,290
When you make that kind of face...

90
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:41,600
I can't possibly stop you.

91
00:06:50,470 --> 00:06:53,410
But I have one condition.

92
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:55,580
A condition?

93
00:06:57,660 --> 00:07:00,700
You have to save enough energy to
look around the cultural festival with me.

94
00:07:05,250 --> 00:07:06,250
Okay.

95
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:09,830
We made a promise, after all.

96
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:31,610
Oh.

97
00:07:32,450 --> 00:07:33,620
Looking good, Mayama.

98
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:35,839
It's a whole new level of werewolf.

99
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:37,820
Should I be happy about that?

100
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:39,420
Can I take a picture?

101
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:41,020
Sure.

102
00:07:46,230 --> 00:07:49,230
Alright, let's crush this!

103
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:50,540
- Yeah!
- Let's do it!

104
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:54,239
Come on, Mayama, you too. Hurry up.

105
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:55,240
Okay.

106
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:57,720
Alright.

107
00:07:58,870 --> 00:08:00,010
Ready...

108
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:01,640
Victory!

109
00:08:02,310 --> 00:08:04,710
Victory!

110
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:08,179
Shouldn't it be "Yeah"?

111
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:09,480
What the heck is "Victory"?

112
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,419
It's about the vibe, the vibe!

113
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:12,729
No, even for the vibe, it makes no sense.

114
00:08:12,730 --> 00:08:13,759
Don't ask. I said don't ask.

115
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:14,460
Why not?

116
00:08:14,461 --> 00:08:16,630
So lame. There had to be a better idea...

117
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:20,099
Hello.

118
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,030
Thank you. Please take a brochure.

119
00:08:21,060 --> 00:08:23,500
Hello. Please take a brochure. Thank you.

120
00:08:30,410 --> 00:08:32,170
I hate this. It's too scary.

121
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:33,340
Wait.

122
00:08:33,420 --> 00:08:34,856
Wait, there's something there, right?

123
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:36,610
It looks like something's...

124
00:08:38,110 --> 00:08:39,499
So creepy.

125
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,150
It's scary enough already...

126
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,336
- There's something there, right?
- Yeah, there is!

127
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,630
What is it?

128
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:51,090
A mannequin. It's a mannequin.

129
00:08:59,130 --> 00:09:01,340
A little louder.

130
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Okay...

131
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,810
Isn't this good enough already?

132
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:06,910
No way.

133
00:09:07,340 --> 00:09:09,500
I may not look it, but I
used to be in the drama club.

134
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:11,240
Please wait just a moment.

135
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:13,150
We're making some final adjustments.

136
00:09:13,950 --> 00:09:14,950
Alright, repeat after me.

137
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:47,760
(Monsters on Break. Resumes at 1:00 PM~)
Great job, everyone.

138
00:09:47,761 --> 00:09:49,650
- Good work.
- Great job.

139
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:52,450
The reviews on social media are great, too.

140
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,640
Everyone's saying the
werewolf is super intense.

141
00:09:55,020 --> 00:09:56,730
You killed it, Mayama.

142
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:59,900
You were seriously
terrifying at the end there.

143
00:09:59,930 --> 00:10:00,930
Thanks.

144
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:05,100
- Mayama.
- I'm fine.

145
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,300
I'm just a little dizzy, that's all.

146
00:10:12,060 --> 00:10:13,060
Since when?

147
00:10:16,810 --> 00:10:18,456
You've reached your limit.
Let's go to the nurse's office.

148
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,980
I'm really fine. If I just
take some more medicine...

149
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:22,450
Take better care of yourself.

150
00:10:24,950 --> 00:10:26,820
What's wrong? Are you not feeling well?

151
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:29,320
I'm sorry. I'll leave the rest to you guys.

152
00:10:35,430 --> 00:10:36,600
No.

153
00:10:37,370 --> 00:10:38,770
I have to go back...

154
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:43,570
You don't need to worry
about a thing, Mayama.

155
00:11:05,090 --> 00:11:06,830
Ah, you're awake?

156
00:11:11,370 --> 00:11:12,370
Ah...

157
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:14,740
What about the haunted house?

158
00:11:15,610 --> 00:11:16,710
It's already over.

159
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:20,480
So you weren't feeling well.

160
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:22,610
Sorry, none of us noticed.

161
00:11:23,340 --> 00:11:25,500
You were pushing yourself
the whole time, weren't you?

162
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:29,760
I see...

163
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:33,820
It's already over...

164
00:11:36,380 --> 00:11:37,380
I see...

165
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:42,730
Even though we...

166
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:46,000
"Yay," my foot.

167
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:47,300
Isn't it?

168
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:03,790
Everyone worked so hard to prepare.

169
00:12:06,390 --> 00:12:07,790
And I ended up ruining everything.

170
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:11,260
It's all because of me...

171
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:15,460
I'm sorry.

172
00:12:19,670 --> 00:12:21,470
It wasn't ruined at all.

173
00:12:22,670 --> 00:12:23,510
Eh...

174
00:12:23,610 --> 00:12:25,540
If anything, it was a huge success, right?

175
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:27,810
Thanks to our super helper.

176
00:12:28,910 --> 00:12:29,910
Helper?

177
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:36,350
Asamiya?

178
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:38,820
You're awake?

179
00:12:39,690 --> 00:12:40,820
Thank goodness.

180
00:12:41,290 --> 00:12:43,630
Don't tell me, Asamiya, you...

181
00:12:45,190 --> 00:12:46,310
It was incredible.

182
00:12:46,330 --> 00:12:48,150
Vampire Asamiya's drawing power.

183
00:12:50,150 --> 00:12:51,150
Wait.

184
00:12:54,870 --> 00:12:56,769
Wow, he's so handsome.

185
00:12:56,770 --> 00:12:59,270
- Oh my god, he's gorgeous.
- Ah, he's looking at us!

186
00:12:59,430 --> 00:13:01,410
He's seriously too hot.

187
00:13:01,910 --> 00:13:06,110
At first, we wanted Asamiya
to take over as the werewolf.

188
00:13:06,530 --> 00:13:07,780
But Asamiya said...

189
00:13:08,010 --> 00:13:10,390
the werewolf belongs to Mayama.

190
00:13:11,350 --> 00:13:12,420
Well, obviously.

191
00:13:12,790 --> 00:13:14,820
There's no better werewolf than Mayama.

192
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:19,560
So I'll leave the rest to you, alright?

193
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:20,860
Yeah.

194
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:21,650
Are you leaving already?

195
00:13:21,651 --> 00:13:23,070
Don't you still have to clean up?

196
00:13:23,710 --> 00:13:24,710
Let's go.

197
00:13:38,410 --> 00:13:39,410
Thank you.

198
00:13:40,550 --> 00:13:41,980
For covering for me.

199
00:13:46,890 --> 00:13:49,660
Right now, you just need to
worry about your own health.

200
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:58,200
Mayama...

201
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:03,840
I guess I'm just no good after all.

202
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:11,000
You don't actually like
this either, do you, Asamiya?

203
00:14:11,950 --> 00:14:14,120
Dressing up like this in front of everyone.

204
00:14:17,950 --> 00:14:21,120
If it's for you, Mayama,
this is nothing at all.

205
00:14:23,330 --> 00:14:24,330
Besides.

206
00:14:25,090 --> 00:14:28,460
I also got to experience what it feels
like to do something for someone else.

207
00:14:29,030 --> 00:14:33,070
I feel like I understand how you feel now.
I'm really happy about that.

208
00:14:38,310 --> 00:14:43,380
Mayama, I took your place.
Does that upset you?

209
00:14:49,050 --> 00:14:50,520
You still need to rest...

210
00:14:56,290 --> 00:14:57,290
Sorry.

211
00:14:59,470 --> 00:15:03,000
Just let me lean on you
like this a little longer.

212
00:15:11,110 --> 00:15:16,040
The vampire inside me might lose control.

213
00:15:17,410 --> 00:15:20,480
Vampires only come out at night.

214
00:15:22,990 --> 00:15:27,060
Asamiya the vampire easily
defies that kind of logic.

215
00:15:30,190 --> 00:15:32,760
Even though you don't
mean it that way at all.

216
00:15:39,770 --> 00:15:43,140
You always take my
feelings into consideration.

217
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:52,280
Always putting someone like me first.

218
00:15:55,980 --> 00:15:56,980
This morning.

219
00:15:58,090 --> 00:15:59,890
When you went to the hospital, Mayama.

220
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:03,390
Your brother called.

221
00:16:06,930 --> 00:16:08,100
Sorry.

222
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:10,200
For bothering you so early in the morning.

223
00:16:10,370 --> 00:16:11,370
Not at all.

224
00:16:11,770 --> 00:16:14,000
More than that, I'm worried about Hare.

225
00:16:14,770 --> 00:16:18,540
I figured Hare would go no matter what.

226
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:22,850
About what happened
to Hare in middle school.

227
00:16:24,010 --> 00:16:25,010
I heard about it.

228
00:16:25,180 --> 00:16:26,740
Even though I only know the gist of it.

229
00:16:26,870 --> 00:16:29,820
Our parents are rarely
home because of work.

230
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:32,520
It's hard for me to talk to
Hare about that kind of stuff too.

231
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:36,230
So I'm really grateful to you, Asamiya-kun.

232
00:16:37,730 --> 00:16:39,090
I didn't do anything.

233
00:16:39,870 --> 00:16:42,706
Lately... Hare looks genuinely happy.

234
00:16:44,490 --> 00:16:49,400
Because of that, he's even more terrified
of ending up all alone again.

235
00:16:51,270 --> 00:16:57,250
I think he's trying desperately right now
to live up to everyone's expectations.

236
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:05,550
You don't have to force yourself
to live up to everyone's expectations.

237
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:10,760
And there's no need to say
things like "someone like me."

238
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:14,260
The day we moved seats.

239
00:17:15,586 --> 00:17:18,016
Compared to when I
first told you I liked you,

240
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,500
I know you so much better now, Mayama.

241
00:17:23,410 --> 00:17:27,440
I've also seen a lot of the flaws
you see in yourself.

242
00:17:29,710 --> 00:17:34,020
I've only grown to like
you even more, Mayama.

243
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:45,560
So please stop saying
things like "someone like me."

244
00:17:52,170 --> 00:17:53,170
Yeah.

245
00:18:04,310 --> 00:18:05,310
Yeah.

246
00:18:18,890 --> 00:18:20,630
Mayama-kun.

247
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:26,030
Are you still asleep?

248
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:30,010
The school is about to close.

249
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:31,410
I'm opening the curtains.

250
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:35,280
Oh, you're awake?

251
00:18:36,650 --> 00:18:37,650
Yes.

252
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:39,310
How are you feeling?

253
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:40,980
Can you make it home by yourself?

254
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:45,490
By the way, what happened
to your face, Teacher Komori...

255
00:18:46,220 --> 00:18:47,220
Hmm?

256
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:53,430
Oh, I filled in for you as
the ghost, Mayama-kun.

257
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:56,460
I gave it a try and it
was actually pretty fun.

258
00:18:58,430 --> 00:18:59,470
Is that so?

259
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:02,270
Hurry up and pack your
things so you can go home.

260
00:19:03,370 --> 00:19:04,440
Okay.

261
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,890
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

262
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:25,330
I can manage.

263
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:30,660
Oh.

264
00:19:30,970 --> 00:19:32,030
What's wrong?

265
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:36,310
I forgot to take a video
of you dressed as a werewolf, Mayama.

266
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:38,199
I only got photos.

267
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,980
Photos are enough, aren't they?

268
00:19:57,630 --> 00:19:59,960
I really want to touch Asamiya.

269
00:20:02,260 --> 00:20:07,270
I want to be the only one who gets
to see this expression on his face.

270
00:20:09,570 --> 00:20:13,080
Let's check out the cultural
festival together next year.

271
00:20:13,910 --> 00:20:14,910
Yeah.

272
00:20:14,911 --> 00:20:15,980
It's a promise.

273
00:20:18,750 --> 00:20:20,826
Looks like the video will
have to wait until next year too.

274
00:20:20,850 --> 00:20:22,450
Wait, are we doing this again next year?

275
00:20:30,590 --> 00:20:32,560
I feel like I can finally say it now.

276
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:38,230
My answer to Asamiya.

277
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,180
See you tomorrow then.

278
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:42,400
Oh.

279
00:20:44,110 --> 00:20:45,110
And one more thing.

280
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:46,680
Mayama.

281
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:48,040
Hmm?

282
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:54,620
You don't have to like me back, you know.

283
00:20:59,250 --> 00:21:00,250
Huh?

284
00:21:00,940 --> 00:21:04,830
I'm perfectly happy just being able to
tell you how much I like you, Mayama.

285
00:21:05,060 --> 00:21:06,660
I won't ask for anything more than that.

286
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:09,700
- But...
- Think about it.

287
00:21:10,430 --> 00:21:13,500
You're like a comforting
presence to me, Mayama.

288
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:20,110
My crush on you is probably like
how someone loves a local mascot.

289
00:21:25,410 --> 00:21:27,020
What is that supposed to mean?

290
00:21:29,420 --> 00:21:30,420
Hmm?

291
00:21:32,590 --> 00:21:35,790
I'm being serious...

292
00:21:37,360 --> 00:21:38,560
Mayama?

293
00:21:39,940 --> 00:21:41,100
Never mind.

294
00:21:52,980 --> 00:21:53,980
You're home.

295
00:21:54,210 --> 00:21:55,940
Are you feeling any better?

296
00:21:58,300 --> 00:21:59,300
Hare?

297
00:22:04,550 --> 00:22:07,320
What the hell does he
mean by a local mascot?

298
00:22:18,930 --> 00:22:22,800
So was this all just me being delusional?

299
00:22:35,780 --> 00:22:39,190
If that's the case, he
should have told me sooner.

300
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:47,600
I've already completely fallen for you.

301
00:24:10,500 --> 00:24:11,200
(Next Episode Preview)

302
00:24:11,210 --> 00:24:17,550
It was impossible for Asamiya to truly fall
for someone like me in the first place.

303
00:24:17,690 --> 00:24:20,160
You need to trust people
a little more, Mayama.

304
00:24:21,540 --> 00:24:23,540
- What is this?
- You'll see.

305
00:24:23,660 --> 00:24:24,990
A karaoke mixer.

306
00:24:25,360 --> 00:24:30,360
Ever since summer break started,
I've wanted to feel you like this, Mayama.

307
00:24:30,740 --> 00:24:32,060
That's not fair.

308
00:24:32,100 --> 00:24:34,319
Does that mean you're
a total mess yourself?

309
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:36,770
If you just tell him
clearly, he'll understand.

310
00:24:37,040 --> 00:24:40,480
That's not what I'm looking for.

311
00:24:40,640 --> 00:24:42,080
Just go home.

312
00:24:42,280 --> 00:24:45,280
At the end of the day, Asamiya
was the one who drew the line first.

313
00:24:45,350 --> 00:24:47,420
Your love life is really rough, isn't it?

314
00:24:48,320 --> 00:24:49,990
I want to hear it straight from you.

315
00:24:50,390 --> 00:24:53,420
At least Sakaki is much more
honest than you at times like this.
